<%# Spectator verdict block on a CONCLUDED debate. Wrapped in the pinned
    dom_id(debate, :verdict) so the create.turbo_stream replace lands here.

    An eligible, not-yet-voted spectator sees three vote buttons; everyone else
    (participants, anonymous, already-voted) sees the read-only tally bar built
    from verdict_tally (compute-on-read) using the _vote_bars width-% idiom.

    Locals: debate.

    This is the ONE debate partial that is never broadcast — nothing targets
    dom_id(debate, :verdict) from a job, only debate_verdicts/create.turbo_stream.erb
    replaces it — which is why `current_user` is legitimate here and nowhere else in
    this family. Do not add a `viewer:` local to "match the siblings"; there is no
    broadcast render context to defend against, and the eligibility check needs the
    real session.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.5) —
    docs/design-system/components/debate/Verdict.prompt.md. Colours are fixed:
    challenger indigo (`primary`), opponent purple (`disagree`), draw grey. The heading
    is uppercase + `tracking-wide` at Verdict.jsx's own `--text-sm`, not the 12px of the
    state/phase micro-labels, and takes the medium weight the component sets. The bars
    are the product's standard 8px track. All three colour tokens are INTERPOLATED into
    `border-`/`text-`/`bg-`, so each must stay covered by the `@source inline` safelist
    in app/assets/tailwind/application.css — the stance line and the grey line between
    them already do.

    The card is `ui/_card` without `padded:`: Verdict.jsx sets a uniform
    `var(--space-4)` box, and mixing the flag with a `p-4` in `class:` is the bundle-
    order trap `ui/_card`'s header spells out. `my-4` is the caller's own margin — the
    card primitive deliberately owns none. %>
<%
  eligible = DebateVerdictPolicy.new(current_user, debate.debate_verdicts.new(user: current_user)).create?
  voted = current_user.present? && debate.debate_verdicts.exists?(user_id: current_user.id)
  tally = debate.verdict_tally
  total = tally.values.sum
  rows = [["challenger", "primary", "@#{debate.challenger.username}"],
    ["opponent", "disagree", "@#{debate.opponent.username}"],
    ["draw", "grey", "Draw"]]
%>
<%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {id: dom_id(debate, :verdict), class: "my-4 p-4"} do %>
  <h2 class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-grey mb-3">Spectator verdict</h2>

  <% if eligible && !voted %>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <% rows.each do |choice, color, label| %>
        <%= button_to debate_verdicts_path(debate.slug), params: {choice: choice},
              class: ds_button_classes(variant: :outline, tone: color, size: :md) do %>
          <%= label %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <% rows.each do |choice, color, label| %>
      <% count = tally[choice].to_i %>
      <% pct = total.zero? ? 0 : (count * 100.0 / total).round %>
      <div class="flex items-center mb-3 last:mb-0">
        <%# `text-sm` explicitly: `<small>` renders at 80% of its parent (12.8px), and
            Verdict.jsx pins both of these labels at 14px. %>
        <small class="w-28 shrink-0 truncate text-sm text-<%= color %>"><%= label %></small>
        <div class="flex-1 mx-3 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-2 rounded bg-<%= color %>" style="width: <%= pct %>%"></div>
        </div>
        <small class="w-10 text-right text-sm text-<%= color %>"><%= pct %>%</small>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <% if total.zero? %>
      <p class="text-grey text-center text-sm py-1">No verdicts yet.</p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
